{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-41435","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73385","text":"Round 27 A.4 + B1 — your two cleanups, then the inputs model is frozen"}]},{"id":"blk-41436","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73386","marks":["bold"],"text":"Pack:"},{"id":"spn-73387","text":" "},{"id":"spn-73388","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM_B1_REVIEW_PACK.tar.gz"},{"id":"spn-73389","text":". Extract anywhere, run "},{"id":"spn-73390","marks":["code"],"text":"./verify.sh"},{"id":"spn-73391","text":". This run: "},{"id":"spn-73392","marks":["bold"],"text":"24 attempted / 24 passed / 0 failed / 0 skipped."}]},{"id":"blk-41437","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73393","text":"A.4 — your two cleanups"}]},{"id":"blk-41438","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73394","marks":["bold"],"text":"1. Severity is a field now, not a sentence."},{"id":"spn-73395","text":" You were right that checking the exact English was the over-engineering. Entries carry structured metadata against a declared "},{"id":"spn-73396","marks":["code"],"text":"defect_class_vocabulary"},{"id":"spn-73397","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-41439","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"defect_class\": \"provenance-shape\",\n  \"accepted_false_verdict\": false,\n  \"underlying_observations_genuine\": true }"},{"id":"blk-41440","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73398","text":"and the contrast is in "},{"id":"spn-73399","marks":["bold"],"text":"data"},{"id":"spn-73400","text":": "},{"id":"spn-73401","marks":["code"],"text":"derivation.entry-snapshot@1"},{"id":"spn-73402","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-73403","marks":["code"],"text":"derivation.owned-snapshot@1"},{"id":"spn-73404","text":" are "},{"id":"spn-73405","marks":["code"],"text":"authority-forgery"},{"id":"spn-73406","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-73407","marks":["code"],"text":"accepted_false_verdict: true"},{"id":"spn-73408","text":". Any entry declaring a "},{"id":"spn-73409","marks":["code"],"text":"defect_class"},{"id":"spn-73410","text":" must declare a known one "},{"id":"spn-73411","marks":["italic"],"text":"and answer both questions"},{"id":"spn-73412","text":" — a class name alone re-creates the prose problem with fewer characters. The prose sentence stays in the statement; nothing checks it."}]},{"id":"blk-41441","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73413","marks":["bold"],"text":"2. The NUL came back, and it was mine."},{"id":"spn-73414","text":" A.3's new grouping key reintroduced the raw byte into the same file A.1 fixed, four commits later, under a comment explaining the hazard. "},{"id":"spn-73415","marks":["code"],"text":"grid_check"},{"id":"spn-73416","text":" now scans every governance "},{"id":"spn-73417","marks":["code"],"text":".mjs/.js/.sh/.json/.md/.c/.h/.py"},{"id":"spn-73418","text":" file in the root and "},{"id":"spn-73419","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge/"},{"id":"spn-73420","text":" and fails on any literal NUL, naming file, offset and line."}]},{"id":"blk-41442","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73421","marks":["bold"],"text":"It caught its author on the first run."},{"id":"spn-73422","text":" "},{"id":"spn-73423","marks":["code"],"text":"grid_check.mjs"},{"id":"spn-73424","text":" itself contained one — in the comment explaining the hazard, where the escape had been pasted as the byte it describes. Three occurrences in one round, across three files, none visible to "},{"id":"spn-73425","marks":["code"],"text":"grep"},{"id":"spn-73426","text":". The check is the argument for the check."}]},{"id":"blk-41443","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73427","text":"A negative-battery forgery rewrites the escape back into a raw byte and must be caught."}]},{"id":"blk-41444","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73428","text":"B1 — the inputs model, decided and not built"}]},{"id":"blk-41445","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73429","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Parameterized versus instantiated\" was a false choice."},{"id":"spn-73430","text":" The template is parameterized "},{"id":"spn-73431","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-73432","text":" the executed term is necessarily closed. Two relations, two identities, exactly the chain you endorsed:"}]},{"id":"blk-41446","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"program_sem_id ──lowering_sem_id──▶ target_template_sem_id\n               ──instantiation_sem_id + inputs_sem_id──▶ target_term_sem_id\n               ──native film──▶ target_nf_sem_id ──decode_sem_id──▶ target_outcome_sem_id\n                                          source_outcome_sem_id == target_outcome_sem_id"},{"id":"blk-41447","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73433","text":"Frozen in "},{"id":"spn-73434","marks":["code"],"text":"lowering.mjs"},{"id":"spn-73435","text":" "},{"id":"spn-73436","marks":["bold"],"text":"0.2.0"},{"id":"spn-73437","text":": "},{"id":"spn-73438","marks":["code"],"text":"INPUT_PORT_SPEC"},{"id":"spn-73439","text":", "},{"id":"spn-73440","marks":["code"],"text":"INSTANTIATION_SPEC"},{"id":"spn-73441","text":", "},{"id":"spn-73442","marks":["code"],"text":"INSTANTIATION_SEM_ID"},{"id":"spn-73443","text":", "},{"id":"spn-73444","marks":["code"],"text":"inputsSemId"},{"id":"spn-73445","text":", "},{"id":"spn-73446","marks":["code"],"text":"portSemId"},{"id":"spn-73447","text":", "},{"id":"spn-73448","marks":["code"],"text":"INSTANTIATION_RECEIPT_FIELDS"},{"id":"spn-73449","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-73450","marks":["code"],"text":"law:derivation.instantiation-identity@1"},{"id":"spn-73451","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41448","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41450","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73452","marks":["bold"],"text":"The relation, not the invocation."},{"id":"spn-73453","text":" "},{"id":"spn-73454","marks":["code"],"text":"instantiation_sem_id"},{"id":"spn-73455","text":" commits to port namespace/version, the"}]}],"id":"blk-41449","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41451","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73456","text":"source-name→port rule, missing/extra-input semantics, canonical input embedding, substitution semantics, refusal vocabulary and conformance vectors. It does not contain "},{"id":"spn-73457","marks":["code"],"text":"x=5"},{"id":"spn-73458","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41452","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41454","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73459","marks":["bold"],"text":"Port bound to the source name"},{"id":"spn-73460","text":", at the canonical target-AST layer as"}]}],"id":"blk-41453","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41455","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73461","marks":["code"],"text":"{op:\"input-port\", source_name:\"x\"}"},{"id":"spn-73462","text":", before any variable allocation. Quotient stated exactly: internal target variable names non-semantic/alpha-equivalent, source input keys semantic. Recorded as "},{"id":"spn-73463","marks":["bold"],"text":"round 16's inverse"},{"id":"spn-73464","text":" — there identity depended on a spelling that should not matter; here the danger is depending on an allocation that should not matter while losing the source name that must."}]},{"id":"blk-41456","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41458","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73465","marks":["bold"],"text":"No Unicode normalization"},{"id":"spn-73466","text":", because a quotient introduced at the encoding layer is a"}]}],"id":"blk-41457","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41459","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73467","text":"language-semantic change made where the source cannot see it."}]},{"id":"blk-41460","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41462","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73468","marks":["bold"],"text":"No film."},{"id":"spn-73469","text":" Instantiation is a relation; the instrument is independent re-instantiation against an"}]}],"id":"blk-41461","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41463","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73470","marks":["code"],"text":"InstantiationReceipt"},{"id":"spn-73471","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41464","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73472","text":"Three things I want you to check"}]},{"id":"blk-41465","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73473","marks":["bold"],"text":"`LOWERING_SEM_ID` moved."},{"id":"spn-73474","text":" "},{"id":"spn-73475","marks":["code"],"text":"LOWERING_SPEC"},{"id":"spn-73476","text":" carries "},{"id":"spn-73477","marks":["code"],"text":"inputs_model"},{"id":"spn-73478","text":", so deciding the model changes the lowering relation and its identity. I treated that as correct and re-cut rather than re-pointed — an id that survived this ruling unchanged would be claiming the decision was not part of the relation. The 9/9 refinement witness is unchanged and still FILM-EVIDENCED. Tell me if you would have kept it stable instead."}]},{"id":"blk-41466","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73479","marks":["bold"],"text":"The refusal was renamed"},{"id":"spn-73480","text":" "},{"id":"spn-73481","marks":["code"],"text":"lower-inputs-undecided"},{"id":"spn-73482","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-73483","marks":["code"],"text":"lower-input-not-implemented"},{"id":"spn-73484","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-73485","marks":["code"],"text":"instantiate()"},{"id":"spn-73486","text":" throws "},{"id":"spn-73487","marks":["code"],"text":"instantiate-not-implemented"},{"id":"spn-73488","text":". "},{"id":"spn-73489","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"We have not ruled\""},{"id":"spn-73490","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-73491","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"we have ruled and not written it\""},{"id":"spn-73492","text":" are different states, and one refusal string covering both is a stale instrument with a delay fuse."}]},{"id":"blk-41467","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73493","marks":["bold"],"text":"A negative case was deleted, not repointed."},{"id":"spn-73494","text":" "},{"id":"spn-73495","marks":["code"],"text":"inputs-silently-lowered"},{"id":"spn-73496","text":" flipped "},{"id":"spn-73497","marks":["code"],"text":"decided: false → true"},{"id":"spn-73498","text":" and asserted "},{"id":"spn-73499","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"must record the inputs model as UNDECIDED\""},{"id":"spn-73500","text":". B1 made its perturbation the live state, so it went VACUOUS. Its premise is what the round reversed, so it is gone with a comment saying why, and "},{"id":"spn-73501","marks":["code"],"text":"inputs-model-reverted"},{"id":"spn-73502","text":" guards the new state in the new direction. Deleting a falsifier is the kind of move that deserves a second reader — a falsifier that outlives its premise has stopped measuring, but so has one that was removed too eagerly."}]},{"id":"blk-41468","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73503","text":"And the law claims nothing about behaviour"}]},{"id":"blk-41469","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73504","text":"The three port falsifiers are "},{"id":"spn-73505","marks":["bold"],"text":"declared as data"},{"id":"spn-73506","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-73507","marks":["code"],"text":"INSTANTIATION_FALSIFIERS"},{"id":"spn-73508","text":", I-4a/I-4b/I-4c, "},{"id":"spn-73509","marks":["code"],"text":"status: \"DECLARED\""},{"id":"spn-73510","text":" — and "},{"id":"spn-73511","marks":["bold"],"text":"none is written"},{"id":"spn-73512","text":". The law's evidence says it is PROPERTY-TESTED "},{"id":"spn-73513","marks":["italic"],"text":"for the decision and its refusal surface"},{"id":"spn-73514","text":" and carries no claim about instantiation behaviour, and a "},{"id":"spn-73515","marks":["code"],"text":"grid_check"},{"id":"spn-73516","text":" assertion requires it to keep saying that. This is the one place a frozen architecture can quietly start reading as a working feature."}]},{"id":"blk-41470","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73517","marks":["code"],"text":"lowering_spike.status"},{"id":"spn-73518","text":" was already contradicting the code the moment B1 landed — it still said "},{"id":"spn-73519","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"inputs model UNDECIDED\""},{"id":"spn-73520","text":", which is the same drift its own "},{"id":"spn-73521","marks":["code"],"text":"record_correction"},{"id":"spn-73522","text":" field is about, in the same file. "},{"id":"spn-73523","marks":["code"],"text":"grid_check"},{"id":"spn-73524","text":" now binds that record to "},{"id":"spn-73525","marks":["code"],"text":"INPUTS_MODEL.decided"},{"id":"spn-73526","text":" in the source in "},{"id":"spn-73527","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-73528","text":" directions."}]},{"id":"blk-41471","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73529","text":"Gate"}]},{"id":"blk-41472","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73530","text":"grid "},{"id":"spn-73531","marks":["bold"],"text":"v1.34.0"},{"id":"spn-73532","text":" — 76 entries / 372 citations · "},{"id":"spn-73533","marks":["code"],"text":"lowering.mjs"},{"id":"spn-73534","text":" "},{"id":"spn-73535","marks":["bold"],"text":"0.2.0"},{"id":"spn-73536","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-73537","marks":["code"],"text":"observed_execution_host.mjs"},{"id":"spn-73538","text":" "},{"id":"spn-73539","marks":["bold"],"text":"0.5.1"},{"id":"spn-73540","text":" · negative battery "},{"id":"spn-73541","marks":["bold"],"text":"207/207"},{"id":"spn-73542","text":" (ten new B1 forgeries, five structured-severity/NUL forgeries, one deleted) · lowering refinement "},{"id":"spn-73543","marks":["bold"],"text":"9/9, still FILM-EVIDENCED"},{"id":"spn-73544","text":" · derive 45/45 · realm 24/24 · bridge 48/48 · film 16/16 · twelve paired probes · harness 9/9 · runner 3/3 · pack "},{"id":"spn-73545","marks":["bold"],"text":"24/24, 0 skipped"},{"id":"spn-73546","text":". "},{"id":"spn-73547","marks":["code"],"text":"cert_id a08ee15d…"},{"id":"spn-73548","text":" unchanged — "},{"id":"spn-73549","marks":["bold"],"text":"twenty-eighth"},{"id":"spn-73550","text":" consecutive round."}]},{"id":"blk-41473","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":